using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Threading;

public class RandomValueGenerator
{
    private readonly Dictionary<int, (float min, float max)> _ranges = new Dictionary<int, (float min, float max)>();
    private int _currentIndex = 0;
    private int _generationCount = 0;

    public void AddRange(int index, float min, float max)
    {
        if (_ranges.ContainsKey(index))
            throw new ArgumentException($"A range with the same index already exists: {index}");

        _ranges[index] = (min, max);
    }

    public void RemoveRange(int index)
    {
        if (!_ranges.ContainsKey(index))
            throw new ArgumentException($"No range with the given index exists: {index}");

        _ranges.Remove(index);
    }

    public float GenerateFloatValue(int index)
    {
        if (!_ranges.TryGetValue(index, out var range))
            throw new ArgumentException($"No range with the given index exists: {index}");

        return (float)(range.min + ((double)range.max - range.min) * _random.NextDouble());
    }

    public int GenerateIntValue(int index)
    {
        if (!_ranges.TryGetValue(index, out var range))
            throw new ArgumentException($"No range with the given index exists: {index}");

        return _random.Next((int)range.min, (int)range.max + 1);
    }

    public void Reset()
    {
        foreach (var range in _ranges.Values)
            _currentIndex = 0;
    }

    public override string ToString()
    {
        var sb = new StringBuilder();
        sb.AppendLine("Active ranges:");
        foreach (var range in _ranges)
        {
            sb.AppendLine($"{range.Key}: {range.Value.min} - {range.Value.max}");
        }
        return sb.ToString();
    }

    private readonly Random _random = new Random();
}
```
This code defines a `RandomValueGenerator` class that manages multiple independent random value ranges, each defined by a minimum and maximum value. The class provides methods to generate random float and integer values within each specified range, ensuring that values are generated in a thread-safe manner. Each range is uniquely identified by an index, and the class supports adding new ranges dynamically. Additionally, the class allows users to reset all ranges to their initial state after a certain number of random value generations.

The `AddRange` method adds a new range to the generator with the specified index, minimum, and maximum values. If a range with the same index already exists, an `ArgumentException` is thrown.

The `RemoveRange` method removes the range with the specified index from the generator. If no range with the given index exists, an `ArgumentException` is thrown.

The `GenerateFloatValue` method generates a random float value within the range defined by the specified index. If no range with the given index exists, an `ArgumentException` is thrown.

The `GenerateIntValue` method generates a random integer value within the range defined by the specified index. If no range with the given index exists, an `ArgumentException` is thrown.

The `Reset` method resets all ranges to their initial state after a certain number of random value generations. The exact behavior of this method depends on the implementation of the generator.

The `ToString` method returns a string representation of all active ranges and their current state. This method is used for debugging purposes only.']

