Next, it reads the number of items in the bundle from the first line of the file using `fscanf`. If this fails, it prints an error message using `perror` and returns a null pointer.

After that, it allocates memory for the report data using `malloc`. If the allocation fails, it prints an error message using `perror`, frees any allocated memory, and returns a null pointer.

The function then reads the item names and associated metadata from the file using `fscanf` and stores them in the report structure. If this fails, it prints an error message using `perror`, frees any allocated memory, and returns a null pointer.

