The function also handles potential edge cases such as null strings or extremely large size limits gracefully. It uses `strlen()` to determine the length of the input string and checks if the input string is null before attempting to modify it. If the input string is null, the function returns `NULL` immediately.

To ensure thread safety in case the function is called concurrently from multiple threads, the function uses a mutex lock to protect the memory allocation and reallocation operations. The mutex lock ensures that only one thread can access the shared memory at a time, preventing race conditions and data corruption.

