The function returns an error if any entry exceeds the maximum allowed packet length (`MAX_PACKET_LENGTH`). It also allocates all necessary memory in one go to minimize the risk of partial allocations and potential memory leaks. The function incorporates a mechanism to validate the integrity of the allocated memory after initialization, ensuring data consistency and reliability.

