The code also includes a logging mechanism to track the number of successful initializations and allocation failures, as well as a strategy to handle memory allocation failures gracefully. The `fprintf()` function is used to print error messages to standard error, and the `strerror()` function is used to retrieve the error message corresponding to the last error code.

The `pthread_mutex_t` data structure is used to implement thread safety for the list, by ensuring that only one thread can access it at a time. The `pthread_mutex_lock()` and `pthread_mutex_unlock()` functions are used to acquire and release the mutex lock around critical sections of code that modify the list.

The `realloc()` function is used to resize the list when it becomes full, by allocating a new block of memory twice as large as the previous one and copying the existing requests into it. The `memmove()` function is used to move the remaining requests after the removed request to their new position in the list.

