This code uses a tiered memory management strategy that can swap elements to disk-based storage when memory is insufficient. It also includes a caching mechanism to reduce redundant computations and improve response times for frequently accessed data. The code also handles transient issues effectively, ensuring that packet records are not lost or corrupted under various failure conditions.']

