The program also includes a probabilistic delay before each packet is added to the list, simulating network congestion. This delay is based on a probability distribution provided by the user, with the default value set to 0.5 (i.e., 50% chance of adding a new packet). The program also includes a geographic routing algorithm that considers real-world network routing behavior, taking into account the source and destination IP addresses, available bandwidth, and congestion levels at different network nodes. This routing strategy can be configured via an external JSON file, facilitating easy updates without requiring code changes.

