The `processFiles` function takes in the directory, output file, start time, end time, pattern, processing mode, and logging level as arguments, and processes all files in the directory that match the pattern and are within the time range. It uses a fixed thread pool to manage resources and prevent [thread starvation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starvation_(computer_science)). The function also implements efficient memory management by using `std::vector` for temporary storage of file metadata, and ensures that each thread in the thread pool has an appropriate stack size and memory alignment.

